{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1450044-trinity-questions-re-inflict-damage-stunt","id":1450044,"title":"[Trinity] Questions Re: Inflict Damage Stunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-28T12:54:08-07:00","id":1450044,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Trinity] Questions Re: Inflict Damage Stunt","content":"Hiya,<br /> <br /> I'm sure this has come up before - and I tried to do a forum search - but didn't find much in the way of answers.<br /> <br /> I recently received my Corebook and Aberrant KS books, so I've been reading up on this new system (I was big on Aberrant 1e and Adventure).<br /> A lot of it is familiar and even some new stuff is familiar, like Initiative. I have Fate, so there's some stuff that's adjacently familiar, but there's some specific things about Inflict Damage that I'm fuzzy on and I need help.<br /> <br /> <br /> So normally for skill checks you declare what you're trying to accomplish like, &quot;I hide behind boxes and try to get to the other side of the room without anyone noticing me.&quot; Failure could indicate that I made it to the other side, but I was spotted and now I have a tail. That stuff makes sense.<br /> <br /> In combat say I wanted to slap a tracking beacon on someone and I didn't want them to notice. The ST could say I need 2 sux to do it; one to slap the beacon on, but 1 complication to avoid the target noticing. That makes sense too.<br /> <br /> What I don't quite understand is hitting someone to hurt them. What an I declaring? Assuming Defense 1 and no armor, &quot;I want to punch that guy hard in the face,&quot; sounds unambiguous, and I think any reasonable person would assume I intend to do damage. But if all I roll is 1 success, what happens?<br /> A) I hit and inflict damage since that was my goal, or<br /> B) I hit, then spend 0 for Inflict Damage since my target has no armor?<br /> I'm assuming B is the answer, but that brings up a weird situation described next.<br /> <br /> Now say that my opponent has Soft Armor 1. I roll and again, I only get 1 success. What happens now?<br /> C) I hit him and inflict damage because that was my goal (though I can't buy any stunts), or <br /> D) I hit him, ... and do nothing else because I have to devote that 1 success to the task and now have 0 left to purchase any stunts, not even Enhancement stunts.<br /> For solidarity, I'm assuming the answer is D, but there's a disconnect there and it doesn't feel very cinematic. In Fate, if I didn't roll well enough to hurt my opponent, I could create an Advantage called &quot;Got'em on the Ropes&quot; so that I could use that with my roll next turn. If it's D in this system, then I can only do this if I roll at least 2 sux (in this example), which means effectively nothing happens if I only roll 1 success.<br /> <br /> I don't know how often a situation like this will come up (rolling enough to succeed, but still do nothing), but this feels like a big bug in the system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26860-saveversus","name":"SaveVersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T15:48:40-07:00","id":1450092,"title":"","content":"The way you describe an action in Storypath is kind of reversal. Before the roll you give a vague idea of the action you are doing, let\u2019s say \u201cI will attack him\u201d or \u201cI will hide\u201d, than you roll, and the resulting successes you use to give details about the action, for example, \u201cI hit his arm, it caused a big cut and he drop his gun\u201d or \u201cI went behind the box, but dropped the things I was carrying and they are now visible\u201d.<br /> <br /> So, what happens with inflict damage, in the practical way is you hit the target, if there is no armor you probably caused a injury for free anyway. If the target has an armor, the impact may have be absorbed by the armor, or the weapon hit the armor and scraped to the side, but the result is, you hit the target and it may even have hurt, but it was not enough to cause prolonged effects, like a injury or even a bruise, like when you hit a furniture, feel the pain but in the next second it\u2019s not enough to make you lose concentration.<br /> <br /> Soft 1 is not a big deal, but with soft 2 you may have 1 spare success to use, that may be used to cause a temporary condition, like \u201cI hit him, not enough to hurt, but enough to distract his mind, causing a complication 1 to attack me back\u201d.<br /> <br /> By the way, it happens a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T16:54:46-07:00","id":1450099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1450044-trinity-questions-re-inflict-damage-stunt?p=1450092#post1450092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, it happens a lot!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, what happens a lot: only rolling 1 success, or not rolling enough to Inflict Damage, so you spend what you have on Enhancements/Complications to improve your chances next action?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26860-saveversus","name":"SaveVersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T07:47:00-07:00","id":1450171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaveVersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1450044-trinity-questions-re-inflict-damage-stunt?p=1450099#post1450099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to clarify, what happens a lot: only rolling 1 success, or not rolling enough to Inflict Damage, so you spend what you have on Enhancements/Complications to improve your chances next action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rolling enough to hit but not to hurt. Not against regular targets, but against some elite and boss NPCs.<br /> <br /> RAW antagonists don\u2019t have armor, they have a defense value and that\u2019s all, but as a house rule I stat them with Defense and armor, that together sum the original value, so you may hit and cause conditions instead of properly hurting, for example. Let\u2019s say the target has originally defense 3, if it\u2019s a tough one I put def 1 and armor 2, while a agile one may have def 3 and armor 0, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}